            "body": "## Summary\n\nSingle-line change in `refresh_once`: non-writer path calls `reload_from_disk_if_stale()` but no longer returns, so execution continues into the refresh lock and full `SnapshotBuilder.build` + `_publish` path.\n\n## Findings\n\n### P1 — Non-writer can refresh/publish (inferred)\n\n**Measured:** At head, `refresh_once` is:\n\n```python\nif not is_universe_refresh_writer():\n    self.reload_from_disk_if_stale()\nif not self._refresh_lock.acquire(blocking=False):\n    return self._snapshot\ntry:\n    build = self._builder.build(self._snapshot)\n    ...\n    self._publish(built)\n```\n\n**Measured:** `is_universe_refresh_writer()` docstring: \"Only worker processes may refresh/publish; web reloads persisted snapshots.\" Implementation returns `is_worker_mode()` (except CI/pytest where it is always True).\n\n**Measured:** Base at `882980b8…` used `return self.reload_from_disk_if_stale()` on the non-writer branch, which prevented any build/publish on web/read-only roles.\n\n**Inferred:** When `refresh_once()` is invoked with `is_universe_refresh_writer()` false and `_refresh_lock` is free (normal for a web process with no in-process refresh thread), the web process will run TMC/chain probes and `_atomic_persist` to the shared `subnet_universe.json`. That races the dedicated worker writer and can persist a degraded or partial membership snapshot that downstream scoring reads via `get_snapshot()` / `load_membership_receipt()` — **poisons-later-row** on shared disk.\n\n**Inferred:** Production boot path `ensure_background_refresh()` routes non-writers to `ensure_universe_reader()` only, so this may not trigger today; `kick_refresh_async` also returns early for non-writers. The hole remains on the public `refresh_once` entry any future or test caller uses under `RUN_MODE=web`.\n\n### Intent vs fix\n\n**Guess:** Title \"share refresh work across web and worker\" may intend \"reload worker-published disk state before deciding to refresh.\" The shape that matches the docstring would be reload on the reader path then **return**, e.g. `self.reload_from_disk_if_stale(); return self._snapshot`, or reload for all roles then `if not is_universe_refresh_writer(): return self._snapshot` before the lock.\n\n## What looked fine\n\n**Measured:** No float/numeric membership inputs changed; no new overflow or grace-clock paths in this hunk.\n\n**Inferred:** Writer-only loops (`ensure_refresh_loop`, `kick_refresh_async` writer branch) unchanged aside from the shared method body.\n\n## Requested change\n\nRestore a non-writer exit after disk reload (return value of reload or `self._snapshot`) so only writers pass the refresh lock into `_publish`. If web is meant to co-refresh, that requires an explicit `is_universe_refresh_writer()` policy change and tests — not an accidental fall-through.",
