          "args": {
            "body": "## Summary\n\nOne-line guard in `kick_refresh_async`: when `UNIVERSE_ASYNC_WEB` is set, non-writer processes may spawn the existing daemon kick thread instead of synchronously calling `reload_from_disk_if_stale()` and returning.\n\n## Trace (real entry point)\n\n**Measured:** `kick_refresh_async` → `_run` → `refresh_once()` (`internal/subnet_universe.py` at head `8595d8fd`).\n\n**Measured:** `refresh_once` still begins with `if not is_universe_refresh_writer(): return self.reload_from_disk_if_stale()` — unchanged by this diff.\n\n**Measured:** `is_universe_refresh_writer()` returns `is_worker_mode()` in prod (CI/test excepted).\n\n**Inferred:** With `UNIVERSE_ASYNC_WEB`, web/idle workers schedule **async disk pickup only**, not chain/TMC refresh or `_publish` from web. Split ownership (worker writes, web reads) is preserved.\n\n**Inferred:** Without the env var, behavior matches base: sync `reload_from_disk_if_stale()` on the caller path.\n\n## Extremes / poison paths\n\nNumeric overflow / grace expiry logic (`STALE_GRACE_SECONDS`, `_eligible_for_removal`, `_compute_membership`) is untouched. No new path writes membership from web beyond loading worker-persisted JSON under `_write_lock` (same as existing reader reload).\n\n## Non-blocking notes\n\n**Inferred:** `os.environ.get(\"UNIVERSE_ASYNC_WEB\")` is raw truthiness (any non-empty string, including `\"0\"`, enables async). Other flags in `internal/run_mode.py` normalize with `.strip().lower()`. Worth aligning in a follow-up if ops expects `\"off\"` semantics — not a gate blocker here.\n\n**Guess:** Full-repo call sites for `kick_refresh_async` are outside this review fixture; wiring + Fly env should be confirmed in deploy docs separately.\n\nNo blocking findings (`never-expires`, `overflow`, `aborts-cycle`, `poisons-later-row`).\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Traced kick → refresh_once; non-writer still disk-reload only | — |\n| owner-rules | Web must not publish universe; writer gate unchanged | — |\n| settled-check | 48h removal / membership admission rules not re-litigated | — |",
