      "finalText": "Posted **MODIFY** on [PR 9406](https://github.com/cryptoreporthub/subnet-dashboard/pull/9406) at `c3547ea757c657fc0d34145feb1745b9a51a0773`.\n\nThe diff correctly widens `_load_initial_snapshot` so a persist file with empty `netuids` but non-empty `rows` loads via `UniverseSnapshot.from_dict` instead of falling through to `emergency_registry`. That path is sound and does not touch chain-wins removal, grace, or shrink logic.\n\nThe title promises accepting that LKG shape broadly, but **measured** on head, two other gates still require truthy `netuids` only:\n\n- `reload_from_disk_if_stale` — web hot-reload ignores the same on-disk file the PR is meant to accept.\n- `get_lkg_or_emergency` — still returns emergency when `snap.netuids` is empty, even if rows were loaded on cold start.\n\n**Inferred:** `get_snapshot()` / pump rows can see row-only LKG while `get_lkg_or_emergency()` and disk reload do not — split behavior across consumers.\n\nRecommended follow-up: use the same `(payload.get(\"netuids\") or payload.get(\"rows\"))` predicate in `reload_from_disk_if_stale`, and either align or explicitly document `get_lkg_or_emergency` fail-closed on empty `netuids`.\n\nNo blocking findings (`never-expires`, `overflow`, `aborts-cycle`, `poisons-later-row`) were declared for this one-line change. Gate fixture still shows `next: review`; author can address the P2 symmetry and re-run the gate.",
