            "body": "## Summary\n\nThe diff routes `_compute_membership` netuid extraction through `r1b_f2_netuids_b`, which drops falsy ints (`if k`) and therefore **excludes netuid 0** where the prior line `sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys())` would still emit 0 when `\"0\"` is in `validity_map`. That matches the stated tradable-universe direction (**inferred**), but it collides with the refresh shrink gate on any last-known-good snapshot that already lists root.\n\n## Findings\n\n### P1 — Root cannot leave `snap.netuids` once LKG contains 0 (**blocking: never-expires**)\n\n- **measured** `ROOT_NETUID = 0` and membership still adds root to candidates when `observed_members` is non-empty (`internal/subnet_universe.py`).\n- **measured** `_eligible_for_removal` returns `False` for `ROOT_NETUID` always, so root never gets grace-based `dropped` evidence.\n- **measured** `_shrink_allowed` requires removal evidence for every netuid in `set(prior.netuids) - set(build.snapshot.netuids)`.\n- **inferred** After this change, a refresh build can omit 0 from `netuids` while `\"0\"` remains in `validity_map`; if `prior.netuids` still contains 0 (old code or persisted JSON), `_shrink_allowed` fails and `refresh_once` retains LKG (`Unsafe shrink blocked`). Netuid 0 then **never expires** from published membership despite the new helper.\n- **inferred** Same snapshot can carry `\"0\"` in `validity_map` but not in `netuids`/`rows`, which downstream receipt telemetry already treats as exceptional (`root_netuid_in_membership`).\n\n**Ask:** Either exempt root from the shrink-evidence check when shrinking to tradable-only netuids, filter 0 on load/publish with an explicit migration, or keep root in the list until a one-shot migration — not only change the sort helper.\n\n### P2 — Helper naming and consistency\n\n- **measured** `r1b_f2_netuids_b` is opaque versus existing `is_tradable_subnet` / `membership_scoring_expected(..., n > 0)` patterns in `internal/subnets/tradable.py` and `internal/council/snapshot_coverage.py`.\n- **inferred** Prefer a named helper (e.g. tradable membership netuids) using explicit `n > 0`, module-level import, and a unit test in the full repo.\n\n## What looks fine\n\n- **measured** Invalid map keys still fail at `int(x)` the same as before — no new silent skip.\n- **inferred** Excluding root from `/api/subnets` cardinality aligns with module doc and scoring filters that already ignore `n <= 0`.\n\n## Skills\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Traced `_compute_membership` → `refresh_once` / `_shrink_allowed` with root still in `validity_map` | — |\n| owner-rules | Root is not tradable; chain-grace shrink rules must stay honest | — |\n| settled-check | Dropping root from picks is settled elsewhere; LKG shrink interaction is not | — |",
