      "finalText": "**MODIFY** posted for head `c1f6dd954a04d4c762832899784321a88b7d3f96` on [PR 9411](https://github.com/cryptoreporthub/subnet-dashboard/pull/9411).\n\nThe change to drop `\"0\"` when building exported `netuids` matches how the membership receipt already treats scoring IDs (`int(n) > 0` in `load_membership_receipt`) and the documented root semantics. The `tag.ts` line is comment-only.\n\nThe blocking concern is **inferred**: workers whose LKG still has `0` in `snap.netuids` may hit `_shrink_allowed` on refresh (root is never eligible for evidence-based removal and is not in `dropped`), get `_hold_prior`, and never publish a snapshot without root—so `root_netuid_in_membership` can stay true indefinitely. The review suggests making export-only removal of `ROOT_NETUID` shrink-safe (skip root in the shrink diff or normalize on load).\n\nGate `next` remains `review` in the fixture environment after the post.",
