      "finalText": "**MC verdict: PASS** posted on [PR 9412](https://github.com/cryptoreporthub/subnet-dashboard/pull/9412) at head `af9a6e08d6e0d56608d0b93aa35e479daa825d20`.\n\n### What changed\nIn `_compute_membership`, membership ordering is now:\n\n```python\nnetuids = sorted({int(k) for k in validity_map.keys() if int(k)})\n```\n\ninstead of a plain sorted list comprehension over `int(k)`.\n\n### Review conclusion\n- **Measured:** This is on the path `SnapshotBuilder.build` → `_compute_membership` → `_build_rows` / persisted snapshot / shrink checks.\n- **Inferred:** Using a `set` after `int(k)` dedupes alias keys (e.g. `\"1\"` and `\"01\"`) so the same netuid cannot appear twice in `netuids` and duplicate rows in `_build_rows`.\n- **Inferred:** `if int(k)` drops netuid `0` from the exported list while root can still be handled in candidates/`validity_map`; that matches how root is treated elsewhere (e.g. emergency rows skip `0`).\n- No blocking findings (`never-expires`, `overflow`, `aborts-cycle`, `poisons-later-row`) for this one-line diff.\n\nGate fixture still reports `next: review` with MC unset; the tool returned `posted: true` for this PASS. The channel should advance Cursor/Ditto on its schedule after the verdict comment lands on the PR.",
