            "body": "**MODIFY** @ head `71f5d4261136370e0fda1a3bc94e1e766d063ab1`\n\n## Summary\nCI-only change: quarantine a flaky SN7 universe scenario. The `@pytest.mark.skip` on `test_sn7_off_chain_but_tmc_listed_leaves_expected_at_127_and_keeps_its_row` matches the PR title, but `pytest.ini` deselects a **different** test.\n\n## Findings\n\n### P2 — `pytest.ini` deselect target does not match stated SN7 quarantine (**measured**)\n- **measured**: `pytest.ini` adds `addopts = --deselect tests/test_subnet_universe.py::test_t9_chain_unregistered_beats_tmc_listing`.\n- **measured**: The skip marker is on `test_sn7_off_chain_but_tmc_listed_leaves_expected_at_127_and_keeps_its_row`, not on T9.\n- **inferred**: Every pytest invocation (local and CI) will stop running T9 while SN7 is skipped only via the marker; the PR title/description point at SN7 only, so the global deselect line looks like a wrong node id (T9 vs SN7).\n- **inferred**: T9 encodes the owner rule “chain wins” (2026-10-25 docstring); deselecting it globally reduces dispute coverage without explanation in this PR.\n\n### P3 — Two quarantine mechanisms for one intent (**measured**)\n- **measured**: SN7 is already skipped in-file; a correct `--deselect` for that node would be redundant with the marker.\n- **inferred**: Prefer one mechanism: either `@pytest.mark.skip(reason=…)` on the flaky test **or** a single deselect/known-flake entry aligned with the flaky node— not deselect T9 plus skip SN7.\n\n## Production / adversarial numeric paths\n- **measured**: Diff touches only `pytest.ini` and `tests/test_subnet_universe.py`; no changes to `SnapshotBuilder`, provider refresh, or grace math.\n- **inferred**: No new consumer paths for `1e308`, denormals, or grace multiply; blocking runtime categories not implicated.\n\n## Suite\n- **measured**: `check_gate_state` reports `suite: clean` for this head.\n\n## Requested fix\n1. Remove the erroneous `--deselect` of T9 **or** replace it with the SN7 node if shared runners require ini-level deselect (and drop duplicate skip if redundant).\n2. Document in the PR why T9 must stay enabled if the flake is SN7-only.\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | No production entry-point changes; pytest config only | — |\n| owner-rules | T9/SN7 tests carry 2026-10-25 owner rules; global T9 deselect weakens chain-wins coverage | — |\n| settled-check | No quarantine policy doc in fixture tree for this pattern | — |",
