            "body": "## Summary\n\nHead `c4ed1e8c6a3dd3c00c706bf68e2af4be9c6a751b` changes only `pytest.ini` and `tests/test_subnet_universe.py`. No production paths in `internal/subnet_universe.py` or `internal/council/snapshot_coverage.py` are modified (**measured** from `get_pr_diff` / `check_gate_state`). I did not execute pytest (**measured**: no run tool).\n\n## Findings\n\n### P2 — Global `addopts` deselect drops the SN7 owner-rule integration test everywhere\n\n**Measured:** `pytest.ini` adds:\n`addopts = --deselect tests/test_subnet_universe.py::test_sn7_off_chain_but_tmc_listed_leaves_expected_at_127_and_keeps_its_row`\n\nThat applies to every invocation that reads this ini (local dev, CI, targeted files), not only an xdist worker shard.\n\n**Measured:** The deselected test asserts the 2026-10-25 scenario end-to-end: `SnapshotBuilder` marks SN7 negative/disputed while keeping the row, then `cov.load_membership_receipt()` (production entry via `internal.subnet_universe.get_snapshot`) must yield `len(expected_netuids) == 127`, `7 not in expected_netuids`, `inactive_netuids == [7]`.\n\n**Measured:** `load_membership_receipt()` implements the same owner rule in prose (chain-unregistered negatives leave `expected_netuids` immediately while rows remain for grace).\n\n**Inferred:** `test_t9_chain_unregistered_beats_tmc_listing` still exercises builder validity for a single netuid but does **not** call `load_membership_receipt()`; deselect removes the only default-suite check that council `expected_netuids` matches membership minus inactive negatives for the SN7-shaped case.\n\n**Ask:** Prefer an xdist-safe isolation fix (refactor the test to avoid module-level `get_snapshot` monkeypatch, or `@pytest.mark.xdist_group` / dedicated job) instead of a permanent global deselect.\n\n### P3 — `@pytest.mark.skip` on T1 with thin rationale\n\n**Measured:** `test_t1_empty_state_emergency_registry` is skipped with `reason=\"bootstrap ordering\"`.\n\n**Measured:** Overlapping