      "finalText": "**MC verdict posted: PASS** on head `ad1c2f6d587f18b55f29e653f625f09195ef56e5` for [PR 9445](https://github.com/cryptoreporthub/subnet-dashboard/pull/9445).\n\n### What changed\n`internal/subnet_universe.py` adds `DEFAULT_CLIENT_SECRET` / `_client_secret_default` and sets removal grace to **0** when `CLIENT_SECRET` is missing, empty, or normalized to the `\"unset\"` sentinel; otherwise grace stays **48h** (`STALE_GRACE_SECONDS`).\n\n### Review conclusion\nI traced the real path: `refresh_once` → `SnapshotBuilder.build` → `_compute_membership` and `_shrink_allowed` → `_eligible_for_removal`. Grace is only ever **0** or **172800**, used in a simple `total_seconds() >= grace` check—no overflow, cycle abort, or persisted bad state from this branch. **No blocking findings** (`never-expires`, `overflow`, `aborts-cycle`, `poisons-later-row`).\n\n**P3 (non-blocking):** `_compute_membership` still mentions a fixed “48h grace” in its docstring; this PR adds no tests in the fixture tree for the env branch.\n\nGate fixture still reports `mc: missing` and `next: review` locally after `post_verdict` reported success—likely fixture lag vs. the posted comment. The formal **PASS** was submitted via `post_verdict`; the gate should advance to **Cursor/Ditto** once that comment is visible on the PR.",
