            "body": "## Summary\n\nExtracting member netuids into `internal/subnets/tradable.r1b_member_netuids_from_map_b` is the right seam (Root is documented as non-tradable elsewhere), but the change is not safe to ship without reconciling the universe shrink gate.\n\n## Findings\n\n### P2 — Unsafe-shrink hold can prevent Root ever leaving published `netuids` (**inferred**)\n\n**Measured:** Head derives membership with:\n\n```python\nreturn sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys() if int(k))\n```\n\nso netuid `0` is omitted even when `\"0\"` remains in `validity_map`.\n\n**Measured:** `SubnetUniverseProvider.refresh_once` rejects builds when `_shrink_allowed` is false. `_shrink_allowed` requires `build.dropped[netuid]` plus `_eligible_for_removal` for every netuid in `prior.netuids − build.netuids`. `_eligible_for_removal` returns `False` immediately for `ROOT_NETUID` (`0`), and Root is filtered out of `netuids` without being inserted into `dropped`.\n\n**Inferred:** Any persisted last-known-good snapshot whose `netuids` still contain `0` (possible on base, which used `sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys())`) will produce a build that drops `0` with no drop evidence. Refresh will log unsafe shrink and `_hold_prior`, retaining the old list. Telemetry such as `root_netuid_in_membership` in `internal/council/snapshot_coverage.load_membership_receipt` can stay true indefinitely even though the helper always excludes Root.\n\n**Ask:** Treat Root exclusion as an allowed shrink (whitelist `ROOT_NETUID`), or record Root removal in `dropped` with evidence the shrink gate accepts, or normalize Root out on load (`from_dict` / disk reload) so the transition is not classified as an evidence-backed shrink.\n\n### P3 — Helper/doc/test gap (**inferred**)\n\n**Measured:** New helper has no docstring and no PR-local test delta in the two touched files.\n\n**Inferred:** Regressions around `\"0\"` in `validity_map` vs published `netuids`, and the shrink interaction above, are easy to miss without a focused unit test.\n\n### P3 — `validity_map` vs `netuids` skew (**inferred**)\n\n**Measured:** `universe_snapshot_feed_meta` counts TMC/probe entries in `validity_map` but compares against `len(snap.netuids)`.\n\n**Inferred:** If `\"0\"` stays in `validity_map`, majority source labeling can skew slightly vs the netuid list that omits Root.\n\n## What looks correct\n\n**Measured:** `membership_scoring_expected` and tradable helpers already treat Root as non-scored (`int(n) > 0`). Centralizing list extraction in `tradable.py` matches module intent.\n\n**Measured:** Non-numeric map keys still raise in `int(k)` during membership build (same failure mode as base); no new float/grace/overflow paths in this diff.\n\n## Verdict\n\nDirection is good; add shrink/load handling (and a small test) before merge.",
