      "finalText": "**PASS** posted on [PR 9454](https://github.com/cryptoreporthub/subnet-dashboard/pull/9454) at head `ae2518217bd4ad0d957ff08f88cc0158efd62a6d`.\n\nThe change replaces the inline `sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys())` in `_compute_membership` with `r1b_member_netuids_from_map_f`, which adds `if int(k)` and therefore **drops netuid 0** from exported `snap.netuids` even when `\"0\"` stays in `validity_map`. **Measured** from the diff; **inferred** that this matches positive-only membership elsewhere (`membership_scoring_expected`, probe/`get_member_netuids` behavior, and the ROOT_NETUID comment) rather than being a no-op extract.\n\nI traced the real path: `_compute_membership` → `SnapshotBuilder.build` → persisted `UniverseSnapshot.netuids` / rows → `load_membership_receipt` and scoring. Grace, chain-wins merge, and removal logic are unchanged. No blocking gate issues (overflow, never-expires, cycle abort, or numeric poison).\n\n**P3 notes (non-blocking):** `root_netuid_in_membership` telemetry can differ from base when only validity_map held root; the edge case `validity_map == {\"0\": …}` yields empty netuids vs base `[0]`. The PR does not add tests in the touched files—worth confirming full-repo tests still match the intended R1B export rule.\n\nGate `next` in the session fixture still reads `review`; the verdict was accepted by `post_verdict` (`posted: true`).",
