          "args": {
            "body": "## Summary\n\nSingle hunk in `refresh_once`: on the non-writer path, `return self.reload_from_disk_if_stale()` becomes a bare call, so execution continues into `_refresh_lock` and the full `_builder.build` / `_publish` path.\n\n## Findings\n\n### P2 — Process-local lock vs shared refresh intent (**inferred** from code, **measured** lock type)\n\n**Measured:** `_refresh_lock` is a `threading.Lock()` on `SubnetUniverseProvider` (one instance per process). **Measured:** `_publish(..., persist=True)` writes `subnet_universe.json` via `os.replace`.\n\n**Inferred:** On split web/worker VMs, web and worker do not share that mutex. After this change, any caller of `refresh_once()` on web (when `is_universe_refresh_writer()` is false) can acquire the *local* lock and run a full refresh + persist while the worker process can do the same independently.\n\nThat matches the PR title direction but is unsafe without a cross-process refresh lock (file lock, single-writer lease, or equivalent) on the build/publish critical section.\n\n### P2 — Doc / API drift (**measured**)\n\n**Measured:** `is_universe_refresh_writer()` still documents \"Only worker processes may refresh/publish; web reloads persisted snapshots.\" **Measured:** `ensure_universe_reader()` still says \"never refresh/publish.\" **Measured:** Non-writers can now reach `_publish` inside `refresh_once` after this diff.\n\nUpdate docs or gate persist so the written contract matches behavior.\n\n### P3 — Entry points today (**measured** in fixture slice)\n\n**Measured:** `ensure_background_refresh()` routes non-writers to `ensure_universe_reader()` (reload only). **Measured:** `kick_refresh_async()` returns after reload on non-writers without calling `refresh_once`. So prod web boot may not hit the new path until something else calls `refresh_once` on web— but that wiring is exactly what \"share refresh work\" implies next.\n\n### Adversarial numerics (**skipped** for this hunk)\n\nNo new acceptance of extreme floats or grace math in the diff; `_compute_membership` / `_merge_sources` unchanged.\n\n## Recommendation\n\nMODIFY: add cross-process serialization before web may `_publish`, or restrict shared work to reload + in-memory refresh without dual persist; align `is_universe_refresh_writer` / reader docstrings with the chosen model.\n\nNo blocking-category defects in the membership merge logic itself on this one-line change.",
